```css
/* Auto-responsive card grid — no media query needed */
.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}

/* Named grid areas for a classic layout */
.layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header"
    "sidebar main"
    "footer footer";
  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
}
.header  { grid-area: header; }
.sidebar { grid-area: sidebar; }
.main    { grid-area: main; }
```
`minmax(250px, 1fr)` means: each column is at least 250px wide, but expands to fill available space — the browser adds or removes columns automatically.

